7. Current conclusion
   The initial review suggests that the largest quality risks are not limited to spelling and grammar. Several documented mistakes involve preserving meaning, following constraints, and interpreting informal Serbian in context. The evidence in this draft supports examples of those problems, but not a statistical claim about which model is better overall. A final report should be produced after the evaluator reviews the tags and numeric results.
